WEBVTT

00:08.258 --> 00:10.593
Are you sure
I can't see you home?

00:10.677 --> 00:12.345
Yeah, I'll be fine.

00:12.429 --> 00:14.139
But what about...

00:14.222 --> 00:17.767
You sure are sweet, Mutsumi.

00:18.268 --> 00:21.104
Let's play on the swings together, okay?

00:21.187 --> 00:24.357
Oh, don't worry about him.

00:24.441 --> 00:27.193
I'm going to pound that idiot
over the head with reality

00:27.277 --> 00:29.946
till he can't take it anymore, okay?

00:32.032 --> 00:33.867
-Hey, Taiyo.
-Huh?

00:37.287 --> 00:38.371
Thanks.

00:45.545 --> 00:46.546
ALARM
SNOOZE - STOP

00:46.629 --> 00:47.630


00:48.465 --> 00:51.718
Oh, crap. I crashed on the spo--

00:52.177 --> 00:55.513
Good morning, Taiyo Asano.

00:56.890 --> 00:58.141
Huh?

01:06.691 --> 01:13.364
MISSION: YOZAKURA FAMILY

02:29.524 --> 02:31.401
-

02:31.484 --> 02:32.986
PLAN 2
THE YOZAKURAS' LIFELINE

02:33.069 --> 02:35.363
Ah?
Pretty good reflexes there.

02:35.446 --> 02:39.993
Wh-What are you doing here?
Not to mention, what is that thing?

02:40.076 --> 02:41.369
Hmm? You mean this?

02:41.452 --> 02:44.164
This is the Yozakura family's
traditional wake-up call!

02:44.664 --> 02:47.167
Uh-uh. You were
so obviously trying to kill me--

02:48.585 --> 02:52.046
What are you talking about?
This is part of your training, too.

02:52.130 --> 02:55.758
If you call yourself a spy, you have
to keep an eye open while you sleep.

02:56.259 --> 02:59.012
<i>No way. I can tell by his face</i>
<i>that he was totally--</i>

02:59.095 --> 03:02.473
Good. Next up, the Yozakura
family's traditional morning exercises!

03:02.557 --> 03:04.559
Huh?

03:05.602 --> 03:09.314
All right. Let's see you dance
to your heart's content!

03:14.110 --> 03:15.111
All right!

03:17.280 --> 03:19.490
Is Taiyo awake?

03:20.617 --> 03:22.160
Morning, Taiyo!

03:22.243 --> 03:23.953
I made you lunch, so--

03:24.037 --> 03:27.707
Now, then, next let's see
you bend and stretch your arms and legs!

03:27.790 --> 03:31.628
I-I can't
bend them that way!

03:31.711 --> 03:33.796
Hey! What are you doing?

03:33.880 --> 03:38.092
Hey. Morning, Mutsumi! Isn't it obvious?
We're doing our morning exercises!

03:38.176 --> 03:41.304
Hey! You made me lunch, huh?

03:42.889 --> 03:44.432
Big Bro...

03:45.892 --> 03:49.145
Okay! We could go on a little longer,
but let's wind down our exercises.

03:51.648 --> 03:53.358
Whoops, not good.

03:53.441 --> 03:54.943
We're making a run for it, you two.

03:55.026 --> 03:56.110
Huh?

03:56.194 --> 03:58.529
Hey, B-Big Bro, what do you mean, "run"?

03:58.613 --> 04:00.406
Hey, but we're on the second floor--

04:00.490 --> 04:02.116
Whoa!

04:10.250 --> 04:11.668
What just happened?

04:11.751 --> 04:14.254
Right, the place was rigged with a bomb.

04:14.337 --> 04:15.338
Huh?

04:15.421 --> 04:17.632
I'll explain it
in more detail later.

04:17.715 --> 04:20.969
Also, I'm going to put
my feud with you on hold.

04:21.469 --> 04:25.139
First off, let me explain to you
what the Yozakura family's mission is.

04:25.223 --> 04:26.391
Mission?

04:27.016 --> 04:29.143
The most important
mission of all,

04:29.227 --> 04:31.354
namely, to protect Mutsumi Yozakura.

04:33.147 --> 04:35.108
It's going to get chaotic soon.

04:35.191 --> 04:36.526
Come on, we're taking off.

04:41.990 --> 04:44.033
Let's go, Taiyo.

04:51.249 --> 04:52.875
I see. Roger that.

04:53.918 --> 04:56.421
I just got a report from Shinzo.

04:56.504 --> 05:00.049
He found a fragment of what he thinks
was a time bomb in the kitchen.

05:00.550 --> 05:02.593
Why would a bomb be planted in my house?

05:02.677 --> 05:03.886
The target was Mutsumi.

05:03.970 --> 05:04.971
Huh?

05:05.054 --> 05:08.224
Information spreads like wildfire
in this industry.

05:09.017 --> 05:12.186
Naturally, your relationship
with Mutsumi is no secret.

05:14.230 --> 05:15.315
MY KID SISTER GOT MARRIED

05:15.398 --> 05:16.566
My account's been blowing up

05:16.649 --> 05:18.609
with congratulatory messages
since last night.

05:19.402 --> 05:22.238
Um, why would they target Mutsumi?

05:22.322 --> 05:23.823
The reason is simple.

05:24.574 --> 05:28.786
Because Mutsumi is the tenth head
of the Yozakura family.

05:29.287 --> 05:31.748
Tenth... head?

05:31.831 --> 05:33.583
Before we
get down to business,

05:33.666 --> 05:35.710
let me enlighten you
about the Yozakura family.

05:37.170 --> 05:38.880
<i>The Yozakura family lineage can be traced</i>

05:38.963 --> 05:40.506
<i>back to the ninjas of the Edo period,</i>

05:40.590 --> 05:43.801
<i>and it's produced generations of</i>
<i>descendants with superhuman abilities.</i>

05:43.885 --> 05:45.470
<i>But among them,</i>

05:45.553 --> 05:49.599
<i>one ordinary person known as</i>
<i>the "head" has always been born.</i>

05:50.266 --> 05:55.813
<i>Though the head has no superhuman powers</i>
<i>as the other members of her family do,</i>

05:55.897 --> 05:59.025
<i>her offspring are always raised</i>
<i>as typical Yozakura superhumans</i>

05:59.108 --> 06:02.862
<i>and can inherit the incredible talents</i>
<i>of the Yozakura genes.</i>

06:03.363 --> 06:05.698
<i>Talents that skip a generation,</i>
<i>so to speak.</i>

06:06.491 --> 06:08.868
<i>The family members armed with talents</i>
<i>protect the head,</i>

06:08.951 --> 06:10.453
<i>who passes down those talents.</i>

06:10.912 --> 06:13.373
<i>This is how the Yozakuras</i>
<i>have always thrived.</i>

06:13.456 --> 06:18.836
<i>In other words, as our head,</i>
<i>Mutsumi is our legitimate leader</i>

06:18.920 --> 06:20.922
<i>and the lifeline of the Yozakuras.</i>

06:24.967 --> 06:29.013
Though, as her siblings,
we don't care about lineage,

06:29.097 --> 06:31.933
and we want Mutsumi to live her own life.

06:32.600 --> 06:37.271
Big Bro, we've been through this
over and over, and we agreed as siblings.

06:37.772 --> 06:40.983
Since you're all risking your lives
for the sake of the family business,

06:41.067 --> 06:44.028
then I have to fulfill
my own mission as head.

06:44.112 --> 06:47.490
Has a finer girl than you ever existed?
Mutsumi...

06:48.366 --> 06:52.161
Here you are,
such a wonderful child, and yet...

06:52.245 --> 06:54.747
What are you doing with this clown?

06:56.165 --> 07:00.753
So anyway, now you understand, don't you,
how unique Mutsumi's situation is?

07:01.671 --> 07:04.966
Eventually, she's going to have to
make her underworld debut

07:05.049 --> 07:06.467
as the Yozakuras' leader.

07:07.135 --> 07:13.433
Which is why right now, her mission is
to gain knowledge of the ordinary world.

07:14.058 --> 07:17.437
However, that also means
that those with a grudge against us,

07:17.520 --> 07:18.563
those envious of us,

07:18.646 --> 07:20.273
those who would use us...

07:20.356 --> 07:24.235
Mutsumi will be exposed
to every kind of villain.

07:26.654 --> 07:27.780
What was that?

07:28.364 --> 07:29.490
Oh, my.

07:41.752 --> 07:44.839
Calm down. This car is bulletproof.

07:44.922 --> 07:46.757
But still...

07:57.185 --> 07:58.311
Stop them.

08:11.699 --> 08:16.287
Could you drive a little more smoothly?
Or I'll spill my tea.

08:16.370 --> 08:18.331
How can you be so calm?

08:18.414 --> 08:22.210
Now, now, we'll be fine
if we just leave it to Goliath.

08:22.293 --> 08:23.753
G-Goliath?

08:27.882 --> 08:28.883
What?

08:36.933 --> 08:38.100
-Whoa!
-Oh!

08:38.643 --> 08:41.103
Seriously, they don't know
when to give up.

08:41.187 --> 08:43.564
How dare they disrupt my teatime.

08:47.735 --> 08:50.905
Didn't think he'd actually show up.
Blow him away!

09:05.002 --> 09:06.087
What the...

09:19.892 --> 09:21.936
You get it now, don't you?

09:22.019 --> 09:25.314
To protect Mutsumi,
who lives in constant danger of death...

09:25.815 --> 09:28.234
that's our family's mission.

09:28.901 --> 09:30.528
From which you're not exempt.

09:34.740 --> 09:37.577
All things aside, you've become
a member of the Yozakura family.

09:37.660 --> 09:40.162
You, too, have a duty to protect Mutsumi.

09:40.663 --> 09:44.417
Towards that end, I am going to hammer
the fundamentals of espionage into you.

09:45.710 --> 09:46.919
This is your first mission.

09:47.962 --> 09:51.924
You are to protect Mutsumi
from assassins all day today.

09:58.431 --> 10:00.099
Morning!

10:00.182 --> 10:01.642
Oh, good morning, Mutsumi!

10:01.726 --> 10:02.727
Morning!

10:02.810 --> 10:04.812
You just made it
in time, today, huh?

10:08.107 --> 10:10.985
Uh...
Good morning to you, too, Asano.

10:11.068 --> 10:12.278
Morning!

10:13.070 --> 10:15.781
Hey, Mutsumi,
did something happen to Asano?

10:15.865 --> 10:18.159
Huh? Oh... you could say that!

10:19.035 --> 10:20.578
Morning, Asano!

10:20.661 --> 10:22.413
-Morning!
-Yo!

10:24.373 --> 10:28.044
Huh? Wh-What's up with you, Asano?
You in a bad mood?

10:28.127 --> 10:30.838
He seems even warier than usual.

10:30.921 --> 10:33.132
Y-Yeah. Look how scary he is.

10:36.510 --> 10:37.845
A-A gun?

10:38.387 --> 10:40.973
No worries!
Even if you end up killing someone,

10:41.057 --> 10:42.683
we'll sweep it under the rug for you.

10:42.767 --> 10:44.435
So feel free to fire away!

10:44.518 --> 10:45.603
N-No.

10:45.686 --> 10:47.271
<i>I decline with all my might!</i>

10:47.355 --> 10:51.484
Come on, Big Bro! Stop teasing Taiyo.

10:51.567 --> 10:54.654
In the first place,
it's always poison or bombs with you,

10:54.737 --> 10:56.614
so how useful would a gun be?

10:56.697 --> 10:58.282
Wha...

10:58.366 --> 11:00.242
But it will give him peace of mind.

11:00.910 --> 11:03.329
Protect Mutsumi from this guy.

11:03.412 --> 11:04.747
Social media again?

11:05.414 --> 11:08.876
Alias: Tamaya.
He's a bomber of some repute.

11:08.959 --> 11:13.255
B-Bomber? Then was he the one
who bombed my house, too?

11:13.339 --> 11:16.550
The bombs he builds are first-rate, see.

11:16.634 --> 11:21.681
I've called on him myself
to help me sabotage a terrorist group.

11:21.764 --> 11:25.017
Help you? But if you know him, then why...

11:25.101 --> 11:27.144
Oh, it's more common than you'd think.

11:27.228 --> 11:29.814
In our world, enemies and allies
switch sides just like that

11:29.897 --> 11:31.273
based on money and conditions.

11:31.357 --> 11:33.693
The only one you can trust is yourself.

11:33.776 --> 11:38.447
Well, not that you
can always trust even yourself.

11:38.531 --> 11:42.076
Never mind that.
This guy has just one flaw.

11:43.369 --> 11:45.579
The fact that he's severely
addicted to social media.

11:45.663 --> 11:46.664
Huh?

11:47.164 --> 11:50.292
<i>Lately, he's been posting</i>
<i>a lot of poems that don't make sense.</i>

11:50.376 --> 11:52.086
<i>But he does post the nature of the job,</i>

11:52.169 --> 11:55.131
<i>his target, and even</i>
<i>how he's faring in said endeavor.</i>

11:55.214 --> 11:59.176
Excuse me, wouldn't you
call that a fatal flaw?

11:59.260 --> 12:04.598
I wish I could tag along, but I've got
to rescue a massive number of hostages.

12:04.682 --> 12:07.935
<i>"Massive number of hostages"?</i>
<i>What does that even mean?</i>

12:09.395 --> 12:12.273
Don't let your guard down.
This one's got a twisted nature.

12:12.356 --> 12:15.192
<i>After toying with you</i>
<i>for a few rounds with lighter bombs,</i>

12:15.276 --> 12:18.529
<i>he finishes you off with one of those</i>
<i>specialty bombs that he's so proud of.</i>

12:18.612 --> 12:19.864
<i>That's his style.</i>

12:19.947 --> 12:22.116
He's announced that there are three bombs.

12:22.199 --> 12:24.785
One is the bomb
that demolished your house.

12:24.869 --> 12:26.829
That leaves another two.

12:26.912 --> 12:29.749
I don't care
if you're blown to smithereens!

12:29.832 --> 12:32.752
You protect Mutsumi
until I get back from my job!

12:32.835 --> 12:37.256
If there's even a scratch on her,
I'll make you regret ever being born!

12:37.339 --> 12:40.009
R-Right. Understood!

12:43.137 --> 12:47.975
<i>Okay, I didn't find anything like a bomb</i>
<i>rigged in this classroom. But...</i>

12:48.642 --> 12:52.813
<i>the assassin might have</i>
<i>already infiltrated this school.</i>

12:53.355 --> 12:57.026
<i>I'm just not going to leave</i>
<i>Mutsumi's side for now.</i>

12:57.109 --> 12:58.194
<i>Hm?</i>

12:58.277 --> 12:59.278
SECOND BOMB IS IN PLACE

12:59.361 --> 13:00.654
What?

13:00.738 --> 13:02.156
What?!

13:04.450 --> 13:06.035
Are you okay, Asano?

13:06.118 --> 13:07.119
Asano!

13:07.203 --> 13:10.247
-Hey, be strong!
-I-I'm okay.

13:10.331 --> 13:11.332
Huh?

13:13.125 --> 13:15.169
H-Hey, Asano!

13:15.836 --> 13:20.716
INFIRMARY

13:24.970 --> 13:27.139
What's wrong, Asano?

13:27.223 --> 13:29.016
Did you hurt yourself somehow?

13:29.517 --> 13:32.978
Uh, no, I'm fine! Excuse me!

13:36.565 --> 13:39.485
Man, what a shock.

13:39.985 --> 13:40.986
Huh?

13:44.323 --> 13:46.325
OUT TODAY

13:49.370 --> 13:51.247
Hey, did you hear, Mutsumi?

13:51.330 --> 13:53.999
A UFO was spotted
right here at this school!

13:54.083 --> 13:55.960
What, really?

13:56.043 --> 13:57.503
It's true, all right!

13:57.586 --> 14:00.381
Not only that, but some kids
say they've seen aliens, too.

14:00.464 --> 14:02.675
They're giants
that are three meters tall, I hear!

14:02.758 --> 14:04.885
Wow, that's really huge.

14:04.969 --> 14:08.389
I heard that they can mimic other humans.

14:08.472 --> 14:11.267
Just now, when an upperclasswoman
was on her way to the restroom,

14:11.350 --> 14:13.143
she saw herself walk out of it.

14:13.227 --> 14:15.396
Maybe she has a twin?

14:15.479 --> 14:19.692
Someone else saw a trash can
moving on its own, right?

14:19.775 --> 14:23.904
Forget the aliens! This is starting
to sound more like a ghost story!

14:23.988 --> 14:25.948
DONE SETTING UP THE FINAL BOMB, TOO! YAY!

14:26.031 --> 14:27.867
<i>The final bomb, too...</i>

14:28.492 --> 14:30.494
...and a trash can
that walks on its own?

14:30.578 --> 14:31.579
That's crazy.

14:31.662 --> 14:35.082
<i>Come to think of it,</i>
<i>watching Mutsumi all day today</i>

14:35.165 --> 14:37.042
<i>made me realize all kinds of things.</i>

14:37.668 --> 14:40.796
<i>Like how she doesn't eat food</i>
<i>that's given to her right then and there.</i>

14:41.338 --> 14:45.634
<i>Or how she's always with someone,</i>
<i>making every effort not to be alone.</i>

14:45.718 --> 14:49.638
<i>She must've learned to do all that</i>
<i>without thinking to protect herself.</i>

14:50.139 --> 14:53.559
<i>All this time, that's how she's</i>
<i>been battling her own destiny.</i>

14:54.935 --> 14:56.437
<i>All by herself...</i>

14:57.146 --> 15:00.774
Hey, Asano, sorry about before, okay?

15:00.858 --> 15:03.027
Look, want this chocolate?

15:03.110 --> 15:05.195
Okay. Thanks.

15:05.279 --> 15:06.280
-Huh?
-Huh?

15:06.363 --> 15:08.908
-You gotta be kidding me.
-Asano? Really?

15:08.991 --> 15:10.242
Huh? What's wrong?

15:10.326 --> 15:13.120
Huh? Oh, hey... It's just so unusual.

15:13.203 --> 15:16.081
You know how you always break out
into a cold sweat or even faint

15:16.165 --> 15:17.958
if we so much as say your name?

15:21.128 --> 15:22.421
Asano!

15:22.504 --> 15:24.548
Are you okay? Want to go to the infirmary?

15:24.632 --> 15:27.593
No, hold up. The nurse is out today!

15:27.676 --> 15:29.637
I-I'm fine.

15:29.720 --> 15:33.724
F-For my wife's sake,
I can't afford to collapse!

15:33.807 --> 15:36.101
Wife? What are you talking about?

15:36.185 --> 15:38.646
Oh, crap! Asano's broken down!

15:38.729 --> 15:41.065
Yozakura! Asano's...

15:46.111 --> 15:47.529
Are you all right?

15:48.280 --> 15:50.449
Yeah. More or less...

15:50.532 --> 15:53.702
Sorry about this. The infirmary's closed,

15:53.786 --> 15:56.080
and there was nowhere else
for you to rest.

15:57.039 --> 15:58.332
Sorry.

15:58.415 --> 15:59.458
It's okay.

16:00.626 --> 16:05.130
Hey, Mutsumi,
are you sure I'm the one for you?

16:05.214 --> 16:07.049
What? Why would you say that?

16:07.132 --> 16:10.427
I'm your childhood friend,
but I didn't know anything about you.

16:11.011 --> 16:14.848
That you're from a family of spies...
that you're the head of that family.

16:15.432 --> 16:18.852
Not only that, I didn't even know
that your life was constantly in danger.

16:19.436 --> 16:22.606
<i>Even with all that on your shoulders,</i>
<i>you stayed by my side.</i>

16:23.190 --> 16:25.901
<i>But all I could think about was myself.</i>

16:26.568 --> 16:31.323
Even our marriage was me
blurting out that I wanted to protect you.

16:31.407 --> 16:34.910
I never even considered your feelings.
I'm just a selfish--

16:34.994 --> 16:37.663
-So negative!
-Ouch!

16:37.746 --> 16:41.834
You've got it backwards.
It wasn't you who picked me.

16:41.917 --> 16:43.627
I wanted you, Taiyo.

16:43.711 --> 16:47.006
You married into a crazy family of spies.

16:47.089 --> 16:49.842
On top of that,
your bride could die at any moment.

16:49.925 --> 16:52.761
Anyone would agree that marriage
was out of the question.

16:52.845 --> 16:53.846
No way, no how!

16:54.680 --> 16:55.681
But you know what?

16:55.764 --> 17:00.811
Even so, I've always wished
that you could be my husband, Taiyo.

17:02.021 --> 17:03.188
And so, Taiyo...

17:04.773 --> 17:07.109
thank you for marrying me!

17:08.235 --> 17:09.486
Mutsumi...

17:10.487 --> 17:11.697
Huh?

17:17.161 --> 17:20.205
Huh? Did you hear
that loud noise just now?

17:20.289 --> 17:21.498
Huh? What sound?

17:22.082 --> 17:25.919
I bet it was just the Science Club
messing up one of their experiments again.

17:26.003 --> 17:28.005
Right, the Science Club...

17:28.088 --> 17:30.966
Wow! That was mind-blowing!

17:31.050 --> 17:34.511
Hey, Big Bro Kengo,
will it be okay?

17:34.595 --> 17:37.431
Hmm. It might be a little dicey.

17:37.514 --> 17:38.932
What?

17:39.433 --> 17:41.185
<i>-</i><i>Hey, Kengo.</i>
-Huh?

17:41.268 --> 17:43.062
What's up, Shion?

17:43.145 --> 17:46.690
What are you doing, lazing around?
Get your butt over there.

17:46.774 --> 17:47.983
<i>Copy that!</i>

17:56.116 --> 17:57.493
Are you all right, Mutsumi?

17:57.576 --> 17:58.577
Y-Yes.

17:58.660 --> 18:02.331
<i>Damn it. I never thought</i>
<i>it would be rigged in here.</i>

18:02.915 --> 18:06.418
<i>But how did he know that we'd be here?</i>

18:06.502 --> 18:08.962
<i>We only just happened</i>
<i>to come to this room--</i>

18:10.130 --> 18:13.050
<i>Morning, Taiyo!</i>
<i>I made you lunch, so--</i>

18:13.133 --> 18:14.176
OUT TODAY

18:14.259 --> 18:16.053
<i>Sorry about this. The infirmary's closed,</i>

18:16.136 --> 18:19.098
and there was
nowhere else for you to rest.

18:19.181 --> 18:23.060
<i>We were drawn here...</i>
<i>He knew exactly what moves we'd make!</i>

18:23.685 --> 18:28.273
<i>Was he targeting Mutsumi through</i>
<i>my movements at my house and at school?</i>

18:31.527 --> 18:33.070
What's the matter, Taiyo?

18:34.696 --> 18:36.031
I knew it.

18:38.033 --> 18:40.452
<i>During gym, huh?</i>

18:40.536 --> 18:43.497
<i>This was planned from the outset!</i>

18:43.580 --> 18:47.668
<i>He was announcing his moves on purpose</i>
<i>to keep me from leaving Mutsumi's side!</i>

18:47.751 --> 18:53.382
<i>And to turn me into the bomb</i>
<i>that will kill Mutsumi...</i>

18:54.883 --> 18:57.761
<i>The exit's blocked.</i>
<i>In that case...</i>

18:59.346 --> 19:00.389
Taiyo?

19:08.522 --> 19:11.692
Hey, good thing
I finished up that job early.

19:12.401 --> 19:15.154
Tamaya's miniature bomb, the Sparkler.

19:15.237 --> 19:18.657
It's super-small and packs a huge punch,
but it has two flaws.

19:19.199 --> 19:21.493
Since it recharges
using the target's body heat,

19:21.577 --> 19:23.203
it takes time to activate.

19:23.287 --> 19:26.540
The other is that
it can be disabled with a single wire,

19:26.623 --> 19:28.125
due to its simple design.

19:28.667 --> 19:30.961
I'm impressed that you realized that.
Good job.

19:33.505 --> 19:36.633
As a reward for completing your mission,
I'm going to let you in on something.

19:36.717 --> 19:39.136
In this world,
where you should doubt even yourself,

19:39.219 --> 19:41.180
there is just one thing
that you can trust.

19:41.263 --> 19:43.473
And that's us, the family.

19:43.974 --> 19:45.726
I would love to kill you,

19:45.809 --> 19:48.604
but even if I have to sacrifice myself,
I'll never let you die.

19:49.146 --> 19:51.106
So work hard,
as if your life is on the line.

19:52.024 --> 19:54.568
For the sake of our beloved Mutsumi!

19:55.152 --> 19:56.778
Big Bro...

19:59.823 --> 20:01.575
All right! I'm going to pull you up now,

20:01.658 --> 20:04.661
but if I happen to drop you and you die,
it won't be on purpose, okay?

20:04.745 --> 20:05.746
Huh?

20:08.081 --> 20:10.292
So what are you
going to do with that bomb?

20:10.375 --> 20:14.254
Hmm? Well, of course
I'll have to return it to its owner.

20:14.755 --> 20:16.506
What?

20:16.590 --> 20:18.926
Hey, wow!

20:19.009 --> 20:20.969
Big Sis, are you okay?

20:21.053 --> 20:23.180
Kengo, Nanao...

20:24.139 --> 20:25.849
Even you, Big Bro Shinzo?

20:26.350 --> 20:27.893
Y-Yo...

20:27.976 --> 20:30.562
Hey, why are you all here?

20:30.646 --> 20:33.815
Oh, we heard that this
was Taiyo's first mission.

20:33.899 --> 20:36.276
We thought it sounded like crazy fun!
Right?

20:36.360 --> 20:39.863
Uh, well... Yeah. Sorry!

20:40.572 --> 20:42.115
<i>Thank you for your hard work!</i>

20:42.199 --> 20:43.408
Whoa!

20:43.492 --> 20:46.453
Come on, you, too, Big Sis Shion?

20:47.621 --> 20:48.622
Big Bro?

20:54.753 --> 20:56.380
You never learn, do you?

20:56.463 --> 21:01.468
I warned you not to gaze
at your own work up close.

21:01.551 --> 21:05.472
Oh, uh, I was wondering
if you might show me some mercy.

21:05.555 --> 21:07.683
Hmm.

21:07.766 --> 21:08.934
No way!

21:09.518 --> 21:12.396
Right, of course not!

21:12.479 --> 21:14.314
What? Oh...

21:18.860 --> 21:20.487
-Tamaya!
-Hey, look at that!

21:20.570 --> 21:23.240
-Wow, so pretty.
-<i>Bingo!</i>

21:28.537 --> 21:29.663
BLOWING UP NOW

21:29.746 --> 21:32.666
ABOUT TO DIE NOW

23:07.135 --> 23:09.721
Thank you for taking me in.

23:09.805 --> 23:11.681
What are you doing here?

23:11.765 --> 23:14.518
Well, you see, uh...

23:14.601 --> 23:16.645
Really!
What do you mean, Big Bro?

23:17.229 --> 23:20.732
<i>You know that Taiyo's house is a mess</i>
<i>after that bomb went off!</i>

23:20.816 --> 23:23.151
E-Even so, Mutsumi...

23:23.235 --> 23:25.404
You don't have
any say in this, Big Bro.

23:26.071 --> 23:29.032
And besides,
Taiyo and I are husband and wife.

23:33.912 --> 23:36.915
The beds in our house
are the ultimate in comfort!

23:36.998 --> 23:41.211
So comfortable, in fact, that you
might not wake up, so watch your back!

23:42.295 --> 23:44.756
R-Right. I'll watch my back.

23:48.009 --> 23:50.929
NEXT TIME
FEELINGS
